191:/// Bundles everything a block renderer needs to paint a block. Passed to every
192:/// [BlockRendererBuilder] so custom renderers get the same surface as the
193:/// built-in ones (selection, caret, geometry, IME composition, debug overlay).
194:///
195:/// Fields are intentionally the union of what each built-in renderer consumes;
196:/// a renderer is free to ignore the ones it does not need.
197:///
198:/// Row-level chrome such as the [BlockDragHandleSpec] surface is deliberately
199:/// editor-owned and sits outside renderer output. Renderers paint block content
200:/// only, which keeps default drag handles available to custom renderers and
201:/// prevents nested table-cell text or inline/object controls from becoming
202:/// sortable rows.
